<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 88,687 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 88,687 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 88,687 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday compared to 108,102 tonnes in the same period on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Wednesday   April 29</p>
<p>    Export cargo		19,559	15,315</p>
<p>    Import cargo		69,128	92,787</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ships sailed and eight berthed. In the next 24 hours, five are expected to sail and eight are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Furnace oil	  25,000	 Al-Safa		   30/4</p>
<p>Lube oil		5,882	 Felice		    30/4</p>
<p>Crude oil	    71,478	 Johar		     30/4</p>
<p>Chemicals	    15,750	 Dilmon Tern	     30/4</p>
<p>High speed diesel  27,500	 Sand Gate		 Due</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
